# How this deck was made (W3C PROV-O): ranked from the sources below, glossed, then checked in the review rounds below.
<#compilation>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-10T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:used <https://www.korean.go.kr/front_eng/down/down_02V.do?etc_seq=61> ,
              <https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords> ,
              <https://krdict.korean.go.kr/> ,
              <https://en.wiktionary.org/> ,
              <https://ko.wiktionary.org/> ,
              <https://folkets-lexikon.csc.kth.se/folkets/> ,
              <https://github.com/bab2min/kiwipiepy> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <#anton-wiklund> ;
    prov:wasInformedBy <#review-0> ,
                       <#review-1> ,
                       <#review-2> ,
                       <#review-3> ,
                       <#review-4> ,
                       <#review-5> ;
    rdfs:comment "Compiled by Anton Wiklund with the help of AI."@en ,
                 "Sammanställd av Anton Wiklund med hjälp av AI."@sv ,
                 "About this record: the comments on this compilation, its review rounds and its sources are condensed from the working notes kept while the deck was compiled (the ranking and assembly scripts, the candidate batches with their lexicon data, and each round's list of changes). Those notes are not part of this release."@en ,
                 "Glossing and every review round were done by AI agents, each round working independently of the one before it on the files the earlier round wrote. The cards were also checked by machine (the app's SHACL and DCAT-AP validators, and scripts checking the counts, ids, Hangul and the uniqueness of every front)."@en ,
                 "Ranking. The candidates are the 동사 (verbs) of the National Institute of Korean Language's 현대 국어 사용 빈도 조사 (2002), whose word list gives each Standard Korean Language Dictionary homograph (눈01 'eye', 눈04 'snow') its part of speech and its frequency in a corpus of 1,484,463 tagged words. Each homograph is its own candidate. Its frequency per million was adjusted towards everyday speech with the OpenSubtitles 2018 Korean word list of hermitdave/FrequencyWords (5,894,996 word tokens), lemmatized to dictionary forms with Kiwi (kiwipiepy 0.24.0): a form's subtitle count was shared among its homographs in proportion to their survey frequencies, and the score is the geometric mean of the survey's frequency and the subtitles', the subtitles' clipped to between a third and three times the survey's, so speech moves a word by at most a factor of √3. Ties go to the survey's frequency, then the number of texts the word appears in, then Korean alphabetical order."@en ,
                 "Selection. The 1180 best-scored verb homographs were glossed, the 1000 best kept in use taken. 이다 and 아니다, and the auxiliary verbs (보조 용언), are not in the survey's verbs and not in the deck. Left out in glossing and review, as contractions of a card already in the deck: 갖다 (가지다), 얘기하다 (이야기하다), 머물다 (머무르다), 이뤄지다 (이루어지다) and 뵈다 (보이다); the non-standard 허다; and 오래되다, an adjective in the dictionaries. The casual 뺏다 stays beside 빼앗다, marked (casual). The last card is 선보이다 'unveil', rank 1006."@en ,
                 "Writing the cards. The back is the word as the survey lists it, in its dictionary form, ending in -다, in Hangul alone, without romanization or hanja. Each homograph is a card of its own, so the same Hangul can be the back of two cards with different fronts. The front gives one to three English and one to three Swedish meanings, the most frequent sense first: English meanings were condensed from the Basic Korean Dictionary's (krdict) English equivalents for the sense the survey's homograph names (by its hanja or its example), with English Wiktionary's sense order deciding which sense is the common one; the Swedish was written from the chosen sense with the help of AI and checked against the Swedish translations in Korean Wiktionary, English Wiktionary's translation tables (the same sense) and Folkets lexikon. The meanings read as infinitives: “To” before the first English meaning, “Att” before the first Swedish one (To become, turn into; Att bli). Qualifiers in brackets tell apart words a learner would otherwise confuse: register (honorific, humble, formal, casual), passive and causative pairs, and near-synonyms in the same deck. Every English front and every Swedish front is unique in the deck."@en ,
                 "Card ids are the letter-by-letter Revised Romanization of the Hangul (사람 saram, 좋다 jotda), without sound changes; a second card with the same letters gets -2, the next -3, in rank order."@en ,
                 "Licensing: the deck is CC BY-SA 4.0. Its ranking uses the National Institute of Korean Language's frequency survey, released under the Korea Open Government License type 1 (attribution), and the hermitdave/FrequencyWords counts, CC BY-SA 4.0. Its English meanings are condensed from the Basic Korean Dictionary, CC BY-SA 2.0 KR, whose terms allow an adaptation to be distributed under a later version of the licence with the same elements, and from English Wiktionary, CC BY-SA 4.0. Korean Wiktionary (CC BY-SA 4.0) and Folkets lexikon (CC BY-SA 2.5) were used to check and choose the Swedish. The share-alike sources set the deck's licence; all are credited here. No sound or picture of the Basic Korean Dictionary, which are not under its open licence, was used."@en .

<#review-0>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Korean and English"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: all 1180 candidates after glossing: the Hangul and word class of each, the sense chosen for its homograph, the English meanings, register and passive or causative distinctions, and the decisions to keep or drop."@en ,
                 "Outcome: 55 English meanings and 1 Swedish one changed (homograph senses, transitive and intransitive, passive and causative pairs, honorifics); keep and drop decisions confirmed."@en .

<#review-1>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Swedish"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: all 1180 candidates after the first round: the Swedish meaning against the English and the Korean, word class and form, spelling, idiom, against the Swedish translations in Korean and English Wiktionary and Folkets lexikon."@en ,
                 "Outcome: 206 Swedish meanings and 4 English ones changed (passive -s forms, reflexive verbs, false friends, idiom)."@en .

<#review-2>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Distinct fronts and machine checks"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: the 1000 cards taken in rank order: fronts that are the same or nearly the same in English or in Swedish, words that are the same in meaning, ids, Hangul, text normalization."@en ,
                 "Outcome: 55 fronts rewritten so that every English and every Swedish front is unique (e.g. 도망치다, 달아나다 and 도망가다; 끓이다 and 삶다); homographs such as 쓰다 'write', 'use' and 'wear' stay separate cards with different fronts. Ids, Hangul and NFC normalization pass the scripts' checks."@en .

<#review-3>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Final full-deck review"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: all 1000 cards, in chunks of 100 each read against the whole deck, by reviewers who had seen none of the earlier rounds: the Hangul, both meanings, and whether the front leads to this word rather than another card's, the fronts rewritten in round 2 most closely."@en ,
                 "Outcome: 170 meanings changed, mostly to tell near-synonyms apart, and 오래되다 dropped as an adjective (card 선보이다 took its place). Every front still unique."@en .

<#review-4>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Version 2: title, description and keywords in German, Spanish and French (AI)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: the deck’s title, description and keywords, translated by an AI agent from the English (the Swedish settling what was ambiguous) into German, Spanish and French, in the words the app itself uses, and checked by a second AI agent that translated every text back into English and fixed what had drifted; the release compared by a script with version 1, which found the new title, description and keywords and the release’s own metadata the only changes, and checked by the library checker; not a human review."@en ,
                 "Outcome: the title, description and keywords are in German, Spanish and French as well; no card changed."@en .

<#review-5>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-11-13T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Version 3: example sentences (AI)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: a short Korean example sentence under each card's answer, written in batches of 50 cards by AI agents, in the everyday polite style (-요) unless the front marks the word honorific, humble, formal or casual, using the word in the sense its front names, in standard spelling and spacing, and translated directly from the Korean into English, Swedish, German, Spanish and French; each batch then checked by a second AI agent for the Korean (the word and its sense, grammar, naturalness, register, spelling and spacing) and by a third for the five translations (faithfulness, naturalness, grammar and punctuation), each working on the files the one before it wrote; and checked by scripts (every card has a sentence in Korean and the five translations, in NFC, ending in punctuation; the Korean in Hangul alone, at most eight words, containing the card's word, and unique in the deck) and by the library checker; not a human review."@en ,
                 "Outcome: every card has an example sentence; the Korean check changed 53 cards and the translation check 126. No front or back changed."@en .

<https://github.com/bab2min/kiwipiepy>
    a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    dcterms:title "Kiwi (kiwipiepy 0.24.0), Korean morphological analyser" .

<https://www.korean.go.kr/front_eng/down/down_02V.do?etc_seq=61>
    dcterms:title "현대 국어 사용 빈도 조사 (Survey of the frequency of use of modern Korean, 2002), word list" ;
    dcterms:creator "National Institute of Korean Language (국립국어원)" ;
    dcterms:license <https://www.kogl.or.kr/info/licenseType1.do> ;
    rdfs:comment "Content: candidates, parts of speech and frequencies. The download page states: “제1유형: 출처표시 공공저작물 자유이용허락 표시 기준에 따라 저작물의 출처를 구체적으로 표시한 후 이용할 수 있습니다.” (Type 1: attribution; the work may be used once its source is stated as the open-licence marking standard requires.)"@en .

<https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords>
    dcterms:title "FrequencyWords (Korean word frequencies from OpenSubtitles 2018)" ;
    dcterms:creator "Hermit Dave" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/> ;
    rdfs:comment "Content: subtitle counts that adjust the ranking (content/2018/ko/ko_full.txt). The README states: “MIT License for code. CC-by-sa-4.0 for content.”"@en .

<https://krdict.korean.go.kr/>
    dcterms:title "한국어기초사전 (Basic Korean Dictionary)" ;
    dcterms:creator "National Institute of Korean Language (국립국어원)" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/kr/> ;
    rdfs:comment "Content: English equivalents, condensed into the English meanings, from the dictionary's full XML download. Its copyright policy states: “본 누리집에서 별도로 명시되지 않은 모든 자료는 ‘크리에이티브 커먼즈 저작자표시-동일조건변경허락2.0 대한민국 라이선스’ 에 따라 배포되며 이용될 수 있습니다.” (All material on this site not marked otherwise is distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 2.0 Korea licence.) Sounds and pictures, which the policy excludes, were not used."@en .

<https://en.wiktionary.org/>
    dcterms:title "English Wiktionary (Korean entries, as extracted by Wiktextract on kaikki.org)" ;
    dcterms:creator "Wiktionary contributors" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/> ;
    rdfs:comment "Content: English meanings and the order of senses; its translation tables checked the Swedish. Text is available under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Wiktionary:Copyrights)."@en .

<https://ko.wiktionary.org/>
    dcterms:title "Korean Wiktionary (위키낱말사전), Swedish translations" ;
    dcterms:creator "Wiktionary contributors" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/> ;
    rdfs:comment "Used to check and choose the Swedish meanings. Text is available under CC BY-SA 4.0."@en .

<https://folkets-lexikon.csc.kth.se/folkets/>
    dcterms:title "Folkets lexikon (Swedish–English)" ;
    dcterms:creator "KTH Royal Institute of Technology and contributors" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.5/> ;
    rdfs:comment "Used to check the Swedish meanings against the English. Published under CC BY-SA 2.5."@en .

